        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "28394b21-188c-54c9-9af2-5a808190e202",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Degville, Richie Furay, Chris Hillman, J.D. Souther, Tony James, Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, Dewey Martin, Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, Randy Meisner, Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper\n- Bands and Projects: Sigue Sigue Sputnik, Buffalo Springfield, Poco, Souther Hillman Furay Band, The Byrds, The Flying Burrito Brothers, Manassas, Longbranch Pennywhistle, Blitz Kids\n- Places: Walsall\n- Topics: pop music, country rock, supergroups, Rock & Roll Hall of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- Richie Furay was born on May 9, 1944 and is an American singer, songwriter, and Rock & Roll Hall of Fame member.\n- Martin Degville was born on January 27, 1961 in Walsall.\n- Richie Furay is best known for co-founding Buffalo Springfield with Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, and Dewey Martin.\n- Richie Furay also co-founded Poco with Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, and Randy Meisner.\n- Martin Degville became the lead singer and co-songwriter of the UK pop band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- In 1986, Sigue Sigue Sputnik had a worldwide hit single with \"Love Missile F1-11\" and released six other singles on EMI.\n- Martin Degville was among the attendees associated with the Blitz Kids scene and later became the frontman of Tony James' Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- The Souther Hillman Furay Band was a country rock supergroup led by Richie Furay, Chris Hillman, and J.D. Souther.\n- Chris Hillman was associated with The Byrds, The Flying Burrito Brothers, and Manassas.\n- J.D. Souther was associated with Longbranch Pennywhistle and was noted as a songwriter for Linda Ronstadt and the Eagles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
